      "problem": "Given that $y<200$ and $t\\ge 0,$ which of the following is an inhibited growth equation?",
      "worked_solution": "An inhibited growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=k(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ for all $t\\ge 0.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only inhibited growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.3(200-y).\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.3,$ and $a=200.$ Note that for inhibited growth, we must have $y<200$ for all $t\\ge 0.$",
